<title>POLAND: MERILL, BIG IN POLISH BOND SWAP.</title>
<headline>MERILL, BIG IN POLISH BOND SWAP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's bank BIG SA sold 202,480 Polish five-year bonds to Merrill Lynch International in a swap transaction worth $61 million on February 12, BIG said in a statement.</p>
<p>The swap will be completed at the maturity of the bonds in February 2000 and February 2001, BIG said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
